# This tree lives in WSL and is opened from Windows. Left to itself, Git for
# Windows checks text out as CRLF while WSL git writes LF, and the two then
# disagree about every line in every file -- which is how a stash of nothing
# but line endings comes to report 35,000 changed lines. Pinning LF on both
# sides is what stops that, and it is why `git stash` failed mid-pull.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Auto-detection usually gets these right, but one byte sequence that reads as
# text is all it takes to rewrite a binary on checkout.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
